+++ b/docs/knowledge_persistence_rollback.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Knowledge persistence rollback
+
+Knowledge exposes persistence through `Knowledge::Catalog.list(tenant_id:)`; callers do
+not query `Knowledge::Document` directly. This extraction makes no persistence or schema
+conversion, so rollback is deliberately limited to reverting the boundary change:
+restore the prior delivery query and remove the Catalog adapter (and, if packs are in
+use, move the Knowledge files back to their original Rails directories). Do not roll
+back by dropping or rewriting the existing `documents`, `embeddings`, or `deliveries`
+tables. If a later persistence conversion is attempted, first capture a characterization
+of Catalog results and all existing job behavior, deploy it behind a reversible adapter,
+and retain the current tables until the adapter has been verified and can be reverted.
